# Git remotes — GitHub primary, GitLab on demand

## Remotes

| Remote | URL | Role |
|--------|-----|------|
| `origin` | `https://github.com/ronanop/enterprise-erp.git` | **Primary** — fetch + default push |
| `iconnectplus` | `https://github.com/Moksh-CacheDigitech/iConnectPlus.git` | Always-synced mirror |
| `iconnectplus-erp` | `https://github.com/moksh-sharma/iConnectPlus-ERP.git` | Always-synced mirror |
| `gitlab` | `https://172.16.200.77/cachedigitech/cache-erp-vapt-31-aug.git` | Mirror — only on explicit request |

GitHub `origin` is the source of truth for **content**. Sync **code/refs only** to mirrors — never sync collaborators, teams, or other GitHub repo settings.

## When the user asks to push / push to git

1. Commit on the current branch as usual.
2. Push the current branch tip to all three GitHub remotes (no history rewrite):

```powershell
git push origin HEAD:main
git push iconnectplus HEAD:main
git push iconnectplus-erp HEAD:main
```

3. Do **not** push GitLab unless explicitly asked.

## When the user asks to sync iconnectplus / iconnectplus-erp / keep remotes synced

Same three pushes as above.

## When the user asks to sync gitlab

```bash
git push origin HEAD
git push gitlab HEAD:<branch> --force-with-lease
```

Prefer matching branch names.

This GitLab host uses a self-signed cert. Local repo already has `http.https://172.16.200.77/.sslVerify=false`. Auth requires a GitLab username + PAT; ask the user if push fails.

## Do not

- Sync collaborators / GitHub settings onto mirrors
- Auto-sync GitLab on every GitHub push
- Treat mirrors as primary fetch when the user said "push to git"
- Sync mirrors → origin unless the user explicitly asks
- Rewrite commit authors / force-push rewritten history unless the user explicitly asks
